   4. To settle it definitively, ran a `--dump-dom` capture of the same page to `/tmp/seatmap.html`, then wrote a Node regex-extraction script to pull all `data-row`/`data-column(-start)` pairs for elements with `data-state="unavailable"`.
   5. **That regex returned an empty array**, which was the last tool result received before this summary was requested. I had not yet diagnosed why (regex attribute-order mismatch vs. a genuine absence of unavailable seats in the DOM), nor drawn any conclusion about whether the original visual off-by-one impression was real.

   The exact last assistant action (tool call) was:
   ```bash
   cd /tmp && /opt/ms-playwright/chromium-1234/chrome-linux/chrome --headless=new --disable-gpu --no-sandbox --window-size=1280,1400 --dump-dom http://localhost:4200/screenings/1/seats 2>/dev/null > /tmp/seatmap.html
